course: dictionary
lesson: 4500
title: Hawaiian: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Hawaiian can be a describing word, a name for a person, or the name of a language. Context tells you which one. «We ate Hawaiian pizza with ham and pineapple.» Here Hawaiian describes the pizza, so it means from or in the style of Hawaii.
explain: «The Hawaiian islands sit in the middle of the Pacific Ocean.» Ask yourself what would fit. A place does not speak, so this Hawaiian is about where the islands are. «Hawaiian honeycreepers all came from one kind of finch» also describes something, the birds.
explain: Some words change when they travel into another language. «Merry Christmas» became «Mele Kalikimaka» in Hawaiian. The sentence gives the reason: Hawaiian has no r, s or t, and its syllables end in vowels, so borrowed words are reshaped to fit its sounds.
fact: «Hawaiian» means from or about Hawaii, the group of islands in the Pacific Ocean that is a state of the USA.
fact: A «Hawaiian» is a person from Hawaii, especially one of the Native Hawaiian people.
fact: «Hawaiian» can also be the name of the Polynesian language of the Native Hawaiian people, such as «aloha» and «hula».
fact: Hawaiian islands are volcanic islands in the middle of the Pacific Ocean, and scientists study the lava flows of volcanoes like Kilauea.
fact: Hawaiian has only eight consonants, and its syllables end in vowels.
exercise: «The Hawaiian islands are volcanic islands in the middle of the Pacific Ocean.» What does Hawaiian mean here? | A loud song | Very hungry | *From or about Hawaii
exercise: Mom says, «Shoots» (Hawaiian slang for «okay, sure»). What does shoots mean here? | Fire a gun | Go away quickly | *Okay, sure | Stop right now
exercise: «Hawaiian has no r, s or t, so borrowed words are reshaped.» In this sentence, what is Hawaiian? | A person from Hawaii | *The language | An island | A pizza with pineapple
test: «We ate Hawaiian pizza with pineapple and ham.» What does Hawaiian mean in «Hawaiian pizza»? | Cold and sweet | A pizza from under the sea | *Hawaiian style, with ham and pineapple | Very hot and spicy
test: In science, what are Hawaiian volcanoes like Kilauea studied for? | Snow | Honey | Sea shells | *Lava flows
exam: What does Hawaiian mean in «a Hawaiian shirt with bright flowers»? | A person who sews shirts | A word from the ocean | The name of a flower | *From or in the style of Hawaii
